@* Moves one thing up or down a list.

   Chevrons rather than drag, deliberately: a finger can hit them, they need no pointer to
   discover, and they behave the same on the kitchen tablet as on a desktop. Drag is a pointer
   affordance wearing a touch costume.

   The ends are disabled rather than hidden, so the control keeps the same width down the whole
   list and rows do not shuffle sideways as you move things. *@

<div class="flex items-center shrink-0">
    <HomeButton Variant="bare"
                Size="none"
                Class="p-2 min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px] text-ink-600 enabled:hover:text-ink-200"
                title="Move up"
                aria-label="@($"Move {this.Label} up")"
                Disabled="!this.CanMoveUp"
                OnClick="this.OnMoveUp">
        <HomeIcon Name="chevron-left" Class="rotate-90" />
    </HomeButton>
    <HomeButton Variant="bare"
                Size="none"
                Class="p-2 min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px] text-ink-600 enabled:hover:text-ink-200"
                title="Move down"
                aria-label="@($"Move {this.Label} down")"
                Disabled="!this.CanMoveDown"
                OnClick="this.OnMoveDown">
        <HomeIcon Name="chevron-right" Class="rotate-90" />
    </HomeButton>
</div>
